exit: 1
--- stdout
--- stderr
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: SENSOR_IP='192.168.1.256' is not an IPv4 address; accepted: the sensor's own IPv4 address in dotted decimal without leading zeros, for example 192.168.1.200
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: SENSOR_ID='North' is not a sensor id; accepted: 1-31 characters, a lowercase letter then lowercase letters, digits or single '_' (it becomes the node's ROS namespace)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: DATA_PORT='80' is not a usable UDP port; accepted: a whole number 1024-65535 without leading zeros (default 6699)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: DEVICE_PORT='70000' is not a usable UDP port; accepted: a whole number 1024-65535 without leading zeros (default 7788, 7766 for rsemx; not DATA_PORT)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: HOST_IP='192.168.1.102/40' has no usable prefix length; accepted: the host's IPv4 address on the sensor network, optionally with /1-/32, for example 192.168.1.102/24
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: FRAME_ID='1frame' is not a frame id; accepted: 1-64 characters, letters, digits and '_', not starting with a digit (default rslidar)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: POINTCLOUD_TOPIC='a//b' is not a ROS topic name; accepted: '/'-separated tokens of letters, digits and single '_', each starting with a letter, absolute (/x) or relative to the SENSOR_ID namespace (default rslidar_points)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: TIME_MODE='utc' is not a time mode; accepted, any case: host (stamp with the host's receive time, the default), sensor, gps or ptp (stamp with the sensor's own clock; the sensor must be set to that time source on its web page)
rslidar-driver: refusing to start: RSLIDAR_RUN_DIR='relative/dir' is not an absolute directory path; accepted: an absolute path of letters, digits, '_', '.', '-' and '/' (default /tmp/rslidar)
